<title>FINLAND: Foreign ownership in Finnish companies up in May.</title>
<headline>Foreign ownership in Finnish companies up in May.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign ownership of Finnish firms registered in the Central Securities Depository (FCSD) rose to 29.2 percent of shares by end-May from 28.1 percent at end-April, FCSD said in a review received on Friday.</p>
<p>Foreign ownership in telecoms group Nokia rose to 73.8 percent from 73.1 percent a month earlier, it said.</p>
<p>Foreign ownership in engineering group Rauma and steel group Rautaruukki rose following significant subscriptions by overseas investors to their recent share offerings.  </p>
